  "title": "PROFINET: Fix protectionMode bitmask upon retrieval",
  "description": "The bitmask in the hfi definition is 0x01, there are only two\nvalues (0 and 1) in the value string, and the code paths assume\nthat the value can only be 0 or 1 (and fail to initialize a variable\nif it's otherwise.) So mask by 0x1.\n\nAlso fix some use of tabs in newly added hfi definitions, different\nfrom the alignment of all other hfis.\n\nFix #20540",
